# Provider Adapters

Interfaces describe MintReels needs. They must not mirror a vendor’s raw API.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — PyAI-shaped interface
transcribePyAIHear(req: PyAIHearRequest): Promise<PyAIHearResponse>

// ✅ GOOD — product-shaped interface
transcribe(input: TranscriptionInput): Promise<Transcript>
```

## Defaults

```env
AI_PROVIDER=pyai
KNOWLEDGE_BASE_PROVIDER=pyai
STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3
QUEUE_PROVIDER=bullmq
```

## Placement

- AI interfaces: `packages/ai/src/{speech,llm,embedding}-provider.ts`
- PyAI AI: `packages/ai/src/providers/pyai/`
- KB interface: `packages/knowledge/src/provider.ts`
- PyAI KB: `packages/knowledge/src/adapters/pyai/` (mapper keeps vendor types inside)
- Storage: `packages/storage/src/provider.ts` + `s3.ts` via official `@aws-sdk/*` (no hand-rolled SigV4)
- Queue: `packages/queue/src/provider.ts` + `bullmq.ts`

## Do not

- Add a local / pgvector Knowledge Base adapter.
- Store embeddings in MySQL.
- Call vendor SDKs from apps or `packages/domain`.
